---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import Palette from "../../components/Palette.astro";
import Delegation from "../../components/figures/Delegation.astro";
import Overlap from "../../components/figures/Overlap.astro";
import Handoff from "../../components/figures/Handoff.astro";
import Routers from "../../components/figures/Routers.astro";
import { paper, bibtex } from "../../data/paper";
---

<Base
  title={`${paper.title} · Jerry Li`}
  description="A short version of my NeurIPS 2026 workshop paper: trees of 7 and 15 coding agents spent 6 and 12 times the tokens of one agent, and no comparison resolved a gain in verified fixes."
  jsonld={[
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "ScholarlyArticle",
      headline: `${paper.title}: ${paper.subtitle}`,
      author: { "@id": "https://yuzeli.ca/#jerry" },
      datePublished: "2026",
      isPartOf: { "@type": "Event", name: `NeurIPS 2026 workshops: ${paper.workshops[0].full}; ${paper.workshops[1].full}` },
    },
  ]}
>
  <Header crumb="Research" />

  <main class="wrap" id="top">
    <header class="head">
      <p class="kicker"><a class="ln" href="/#research">Research</a></p>
      <h1>{paper.title}</h1>
      <p class="sub">{paper.subtitle}</p>
      <p class="meta">
        Jerry Li, sole author. Accepted at two NeurIPS 2026 workshops in Sydney:{" "}
        {paper.workshops[0].full}, and {paper.workshops[1].full}.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2 id="question">The question</h2>
      <p>
        A coding agent can do a task itself, or spawn other agents, hand them pieces, and merge what
        comes back. Does a tree of agents that costs several times as much deliver more correct work?
      </p>

      <h2 id="experiment">The experiment</h2>
      <p>
        Two campaigns on DeepSWE: repository repairs from public GitHub projects in five languages,
        97 of 113 tasks gradable. A fix counts only if an external verifier passes every failing test
        and breaks none. Every comparison is between arms on the same task, with one model
        (gpt-5.6-luna), fixed prompts, tools and per-agent turn budget, and a 6,000,000-token cap
        that never bound. Run order is randomised; intervals are bootstrapped over repositories.
      </p>
      <p>
        The depth campaign varies the tree: one agent, then balanced trees of 3, 7 and 15. The return
        campaign fixes it at seven and changes only what workers hand back.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="plate wide"><Delegation n={1} /></div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2 id="cost">1. Trees cost more, with no resolved gain</h2>
      <p>
        Trees of 7 and 15 agents spent 5.98 and 12.50 times the tokens of one agent. Verified success
        did not follow: −4.00 points (95% interval −15.09 to +8.00) at 7 agents and −6.03 (−16.96 to
        +5.56) at 15, and the 3-agent tree was resolvably worse at −11.54 (−20.93 to −2.05). A verified
        fix cost $0.58 with one agent and $6.92 with 15.
      </p>

      <h2 id="overlap">2. The tree repeats its own work</h2>
      <p>
        Explicit coordination is under a fifth of a percent of the tokens, so the cost is not
        overhead. Sibling agents touch the same files more often than the task alone predicts,
        by 9.8 points (5.0 to 15.1) at 7 agents, and 149 of 165 patches a parent refused, 90.3%,
        collide line for line when replayed.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="plate"><Overlap n={2} /></div>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        If merging is the bottleneck, one writer should fix it. In the return campaign workers handed
        back written findings and only the root wrote code. That removed every shared write and moved
        verified success by +1.25 points (−9.76 to +12.82). The design had 80% power at a 16.1-point
        effect, so this is unresolved, not proof of no effect.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="plate"><Handoff n={3} /></div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2 id="routers">3. No tested router resolved an advantage</h2>
      <p>
        Delegating only where it helps would rescue the average. Routers trained on 23 features known
        before a run and tested on unseen repositories did not: none beat the best constant choice
        with an interval excluding zero (best +0.037, −0.036 to +0.125), and one fitted router chose
        the single agent for all 39 tasks.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="plate"><Routers n={4} /></div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2 id="limits">Scope and limits</h2>
      <p>
        For this model, harness, benchmark and budget, one agent is the defensible default. The cost
        multiple is precise; the correctness return is bounded but unresolved, and a larger
        study could still find a modest effect either way. Nothing here speaks to other models, flat
        teams or other ways to merge. A harness that watches for overlap once workers start could stop
        paying for branches that find nothing new. I did not build that controller.
      </p>

      <h2 id="cite">Cite</h2>
      <p>
        The camera-ready version is not public yet. For the manuscript,{" "}
        <a class="ln" href="mailto:fireheartjerry@gmail.com">email me</a>.
      </p>
      <pre class="bib" data-bib>{bibtex}</pre>
      <p class="tools">
        <button type="button" class="ln" data-copy-bib>Copy BibTeX</button>
        <span class="said" aria-live="polite" data-said></span>
      </p>
      <p class="back"><a class="ln" href="/#research">Back to research</a></p>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer n={5} />
  <Palette
    local={[
      { label: "The question", href: "#question" },
      { label: "The experiment", href: "#experiment", keys: "method design setup model benchmark deepswe" },
      { label: "Trees cost more, with no resolved gain", href: "#cost", keys: "finding one tokens depth" },
      { label: "The tree repeats its own work", href: "#overlap", keys: "finding two overlap handoff merge" },
      { label: "No tested router resolved an advantage", href: "#routers", keys: "finding three routing policy" },
      { label: "Scope and limits", href: "#limits", keys: "limitations caveats" },
      { label: "Cite", href: "#cite", keys: "bibtex citation reference" },
    ]}
  />

  <script>
    import "../../scripts/figures";

    const btn = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-copy-bib]");
    const said = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-said]");
    const bib = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-bib]");
    btn?.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(bib!.textContent ?? "");
        said!.textContent = "Copied";
      } catch {
        // Clipboard blocked: select the entry so it can be copied by hand.
        getSelection()?.selectAllChildren(bib!);
        said!.textContent = "Selected; press copy";
      }
      window.setTimeout(() => (said!.textContent = ""), 1800);
    });
  </script>
</Base>

<style>
  main {
    padding-top: clamp(48px, 8vw, 112px);
  }
  .head {
    max-width: 880px;
  }
  .kicker {
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .kicker a {
    padding-block: 10px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(40px, 6.4vw, 96px);
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: -0.042em;
  }
  .sub {
    margin-top: 18px;
    font-size: clamp(19px, 1.62vw, 23px);
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.012em;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    max-width: 30ch;
  }
  .meta {
    margin-top: 22px;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    max-width: 62ch;
  }
  .prose {
    max-width: 660px;
    margin-top: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px);
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .prose h2 {
    font-size: 21px;
    line-height: 1.25;
    letter-spacing: -0.012em;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-top: 1.9em;
  }
  .prose h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .prose p {
    margin-top: 0.75em;
  }
  .prose p :global(a.ln) {
    padding-block: 10px;
  }
  .plate {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin-top: clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px);
  }
  .plate.wide {
    max-width: none;
  }
  .bib {
    margin: 14px 0 0;
    padding: 16px 18px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    font: 13.5px/1.6 ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, monospace;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    background: var(--panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--hair);
    border-radius: 9px;
  }
  /* On a narrow screen the entry wraps, so no line runs out of sight. */
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .bib {
      white-space: pre-wrap;
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }
  }
  .tools {
    display: flex;
    gap: 14px;
    align-items: baseline;
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .tools button {
    padding-block: 10px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .said {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .back {
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .back a {
    padding-block: 10px;
  }
</style>
